[statement]
A package whose condition names a name packages only provide does not
steer the choice of the provider that completes it: `top` needs `D`,
which `d3` provides with a priority of 10 and `d1` with none; `a`'s
condition is `D`, and `a` needs `w`, which only `d1` provides. apk takes
`d3` for `D`, and `d1` for `a` beside it. Contrast
`a-package-whose-condition-holds-does-not-steer-the-choice-completing-it`,
where the provider of `w` cannot be installed beside the choice.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:D

P:a
V:1
D:w
i:D

P:d3
V:1
k:10
p:D

P:d1
V:1
p:D w=2

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install d3 1
install d1 1
install a 1
install top 1
